      <slug></slug>
      <title>AHAH crash course</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Drupal</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Implementing AHAH (Asynchronous HTML and HTTP) requires some Form API voodoo to get it done right. At first instance it can be hard to get a grasp at the concepts of AHAH. If you&amp;#39;re a novice to AHAH, it&amp;#39;s really easy to implement it wrong and hurt the Form API.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Wim Leers&amp;#39; AHAH helper module simplifies the implementation and with his Hierarchical Select module AHAH can be taken even further. This presentation wraps up everything AHAH.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="771">Matthias Vandermaesen</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>